{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Why will you be struck.</b> The tav of תכו is like the tav of לרגליך (Deuteronomy 33:3); the root is like ושפו עצמותיו (Job 33:21), and in this place it is in the direct address [לנוכח], and the meaning is: whatever you are struck, you still add to rebel, for the proper thing was to do repentance, like ובעת הצר לו ויוסף למעול (II Chronicles 28:22 [sic]):" "<b>Sickness.</b> It lacks a word or thing, from the root of סורר (Deuteronomy 21:18). Or it may be a noun:" "<b>Every head to sickness.</b> He explains: על מה תכו, for every head is ready for every sickness. And he mentioned the head and the heart, for both of them are the chiefs:" "<b>Afflicted.</b> An adjective like גנב (Psalms 50:18), סלח (ibid. 86:5):"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The verse cited as II Chronicles 26:22 is actually II Chronicles 28:22; the citation may reflect a variant numbering or copyist error."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:51:36.556413466Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}